# Test: a plugin command with no YANG node is offered and runs from the admin console
# VALIDATES: spec-command-surface-parity, web admin arm for plugin commands.
# The fakeenrich test plugin declares `show test enrich` in its Stage 1
# registration (internal/test/plugins/fakeenrich, commandDecls) and no YANG
# module holds that path. The admin tree is the YANG tree overlaid per request
# with the daemon's plugin commands (cmd/ze/hub/service_web.go
# adminCommandTrees), so `/admin/show/test` lists `enrich`, and executing it
# returns the plugin's answer, whose `source` is `fakeenrich-handler`.
# PREVENTS: the admin console offering only YANG nodes, so a third-party
# plugin's command is reachable from SSH and the API but not from the web.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=server:kind=daemon
option=plugin:name=fakeenrich

# The child link, not the bare word: element:text matches the whole
# accessibility snapshot, so an exact href is the anchor.
action=open:path=/admin/show/test
expect=html:contains=href="/admin/show/test/enrich/"
action=open:path=/admin/show/test/enrich
# The heading names the URL path and renders even for a path no node holds:
# it proves the navigation landed, not that the command exists.
expect=element:text=show test enrich
action=click:text=Execute
expect=element:text=fakeenrich-handler
expect=element:not-text=panic
